Source: Linux stable, branch linux-6.12.y (github.com/gregkh/linux), fetched 2026-11-15
These files are kept exactly as upstream has them. The module does not compile
them directly: scripts/gen-scx61.py turns ext.c into the android14-6.1 port,
and cpumask.c into the cpumask kfuncs, which arrived in v6.3 and which nearly
every scheduler calls.

6.12 is the oldest release the sched-ext/scx headers still wrap (the kfuncs are
scx_bpf_dispatch and scx_bpf_consume there), so schedulers built from current
sources bind to it through upstream's own compat layer.

